## Logical roadmap

Sequencing only — does not assume a specific destination stack.
Rationale: deliver each phase behind a working artifact so progress
is observable.

### Sprint 1 — Read & classify (foundation)

1. Land `learning-path.md` walkthrough for the team.
2. Confirm `reuse-checklist.md` decisions for all Tier 1.
3. Open ADRs in `decisions.md` marked `inviolable` — extract
   invariant tests for your test suite.

### Sprint 2 — Implement Tier 1 (highest priority items only)

4. Walk `implementation-guide.md` for the top Tier 1 component.
5. Set up Time A (spec) and Time B (clean-room) or run A-only.
6. Validate against `extract/components.md` row.

### Sprint 3 — Wrap Tier 2 + clean-room Tier 1 (second pass)

7. For Tier 2 components marked `wrap`, draft adapters.
8. For Tier 1 components marked `clean-room`, run the
   implementation guide through the team.
9. Re-score if any C3 (license) or C4 (velocity) changed during
   the cycle.

### Sprint 4 — Defer / skip Tier 3 + close audit

10. Confirm Tier 3 `skip` decisions still hold.
11. Update `risk-raw.md` with skip-justifications.
12. Run `validator.py check <system>` for a final go/no-go.

> **Note**: the sprint names are illustrative. Replace with the
> team's actual sprint cadence. The sequencing principle
> (foundation → Tier 1 wrap → Tier 2 wrap → Tier 3 cleanup) is the
> load-bearing part.

